# Wiki controls

- Strict types and schema validation; sanitize stored/rendered HTML and authorize edits server-side.
- No placeholder articles, simulated migration/publish success, fake health, or silent fallback.
- Preserve content history and links; migrations require backup, rehearsal, compatibility, and rollback.
- Meet WCAG 2.2 AA and test search, navigation, article rendering, editing, auth, and failure states.
- Run article validation, type-check, tests when present, and build. Missing tests are a reported gap.
- Production requires immutable artifact, approval, rollback, and post-deploy evidence.
